Package: fastsaegpu
Type: Package
Title: GPU-Accelerated Hierarchical Bayesian Small Area Estimation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ridson", "Al Farizal P", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "alfrzlp@gmail.com")
Description: Hierarchical Bayesian area-level Small Area Estimation (SAE)
    based on the Fay-Herriot model (Fay and Herriot, 1979)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1979.10482505>, with spatio-temporal dynamics
    powered by 'NumPyro' (Phan et al., 2019) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1912.11554>
    and 'JAX' <https://jax.readthedocs.io/> on NVIDIA 'CUDA' GPUs or the
    CPU (the Apple Silicon 'Metal' backend cannot yet run the NUTS sampler,
    so it falls back to the CPU). Provides spatial, temporal, and
    spatio-temporal interactions for continuous, count, and bounded survey
    outcomes using Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) sampling, plus mixed
    effects random forests, generalized variance functions, and benchmarking.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/ridsonap/fastsae-gpu
BugReports: https://github.com/ridsonap/fastsae-gpu/issues
